  "body": "### Description\n\nAfter the latest update today I encounter problems with setting up the security key\r\n\r\nFirst I have no idea WHY a securtity key is needed, the user has his/her password which is enough\r\n\r\nMy installation:\r\nTwo homeservers connected with HAPROXY to get one acces IPaddress\r\nUbuntu 20.04-5 including latest updates\r\nPostgres database but unable to setup replication as this is a complicated and difficult process\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- list the steps\r\n- -After updating matrix  to version 1.72+focal+1 after login I get the question for a security key\r\n- I did a full reset to create the key and copied it\r\n- Continue the login I needed to enter this key again and get wrong key.\r\n\r\n\n\n### Homeserver\n\nubuntu 20.04-5 with elements and matrix synapse 1.72+focal+1\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.72 focal+1\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\n\n### Database\n\nuse postgreSQL not replicated, no backups used\n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nTwo single servers\r\nNo dockers, just plain debian packages\n\n### Configuration\n\nAll is standerd installation\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nNo bug reports\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\nnope",
